# Something that can be seen happens before the throw: in a callee that calls itself, in a helper that catches, in a constructor that is copied into the loop, in one that is called, and in a try of the loop, of whose two throws
# one stands behind it. No iteration restarts behind those catches. restarts-behind-caught-throws.ir holds what may.
